    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0146" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">855.001 Leopold/10–145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Patterson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-01T13:00:00+01:00">October 1, 1945—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1216. US military authorities confirm King Leopold expected depart Saint Wolfgang
                    for Switzerland 9 this morning. Convoy with baggage and part household actually
                    started journey yesterday morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Patterson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
